							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">thanks for posting this article<br /><br />I hit Barnes and Nobles the other night, grabbed &quot;A Peoples History&quot; (which they only had hardcover, didnt really have the money to blow on it), so I just sat down for an hour and read for a bit, and just had to drop the dough on it....the book is a crazy read so far.  Many reviews I checked out beforehand criticized the fast pace and use of quotes and letters to display a one sided story, but when you see examples like Powhatan&#039;s letter to John Smith, its really a shame how one sided these events were portrayed in the first place.  Props for posting this and putting me on to Zinn, cant wait to tear down these next 600 pages.  </div>
